! Proposed Definitions And Examples


!! Proposed Definition of ''do''

;__do__ (KOhA3): you -- pro-sumti: you listener(s); identified by vocative -- can mean second-person singular or second-person plural. 
** Keywords: you, y'all

!! Examples of ''do'' Usage

mi pendo do - - I am a friend of you.

!! Proposed Definition of ''do'o''

;__do'o__ (KOhA3): you and others -- pro-sumti: you the listener & others unspecified -- means second and third person together.
** Keywords: "you and them"

!! Examples of ''do'o'' Usage

mi sidju do'o - - I help you and them.

!! Proposed Definition of ''ko''

;__ko__ (KOhA3): imperative -- pro-sumti: you (imperative); make it true for you, the listener --
** Keywords:

!! Examples of ''ko'' Usage

ko sarji la lojban - - Support Lojban.

!! Proposed Definition of ''ma'a''

;__ma'a__ (KOhA3): we with you -- pro-sumti: me/we the speaker(s)/author(s) & you the listener(s) & others unspecified --
** Keywords: "me/we, you/y'all, and him/her/them" "us" "we"

!! Examples of ''ma'a'' Usage

ma'a xusra du'u lei jetnu - - We (meaning the signatories of the Declaration of Independence, the American reader, and the citizens of the nation) hold these truths.

!! Proposed Definition of ''mi''

;__mi__ (KOhA3): me -- pro-sumti: me/we the speaker(s)/author(s); identified by self-vocative --
** Keywords:

!! Examples of ''mi'' Usage

!! Proposed Definition of ''mi'a''

;__mi'a__ (KOhA3): we, not you -- pro-sumti: me/we the speaker(s)/author(s) & others unspecified, but not you, the listener --
** Keywords:

!! Examples of ''mi'a'' Usage

!! Proposed Definition of ''mi'o''

;__mi'o__ (KOhA3): me and you -- pro-sumti: me/we the speaker(s)/author(s) & you the listener(s) --
** Keywords:

!! Examples of ''mi'o'' Usage

